/* =============================================================================
 *  Lambda pre-compile — the one build step GraphQL forces on us.
 * =============================================================================
 *  SST bundles Lambdas with esbuild, and esbuild does not implement
 *  `emitDecoratorMetadata` (it's a type-directed emit, and esbuild deliberately
 *  doesn't type-check). Most of this repo copes by never relying on it: gateways
 *  and services inject with an explicit `@Inject(Token)`.
 *
 *  @nestjs/graphql can't cope the same way — `@Args()` unconditionally reads
 *  `design:paramtypes[index]`, so with no metadata the schema build dies during
 *  app.init() with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')`, which
 *  reaches the client as a bare 502 on the WebSocket handshake.
 *
 *  So: run the real TypeScript compiler first (it DOES emit the metadata) and
 *  point SST's handler at the compiled JS. esbuild then just bundles JS whose
 *  __metadata() calls are already baked in.
 *
 *  Output mirrors src/, so the example's `require('../../..')` still resolves to
 *  .lambda/index.js and `require('../../../graphql')` to .lambda/graphql/index.js.
 * ========================================================================== */
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": ".lambda",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "declaration": false,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "noEmit": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"]
}
